  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nThe extended stretch of dry and pleasant weather will continue\nacross the region with mostly sunny and warm conditions today,\nwith low/mid 70s across the lowlands (~10 degrees above \nnormal). A weak cold front, currently across the central Great \nLakes, will move southward into the area overnight, eventually \nclearing the CWA to the south during the day on Friday. The\nfront will pass through mainly dry, with just the chance for a\nfew isolated showers across the northern mountains w/ increased\nlift via land-forced ascent late tonight into Friday morning. \nOtherwise, patchy river valley fog across the deeper valleys of \nsouthern WV and southwest VA is expected later tonight, with \nincreased BL flow further preventing fog formation overnight. \n\nThereafter, dry weather is expected area-wide through Saturday\ncourtesy of high pressure traversing north of the region, with \nhigh temperatures generally 5-10 degrees cooler than today, \nalbeit still above normal. The next chance for ISOLD to perhaps \nSCT showers returns late Sunday into Monday as a mid/upper level\nwave moves across the region. PoPs have steadily decreased the \nlast couple of days in association with this, now generally in \nthe 15-30% range, with dry low-levels being an inhibiting \nfactor. Highs Sunday/Monday are progged for the upper 60s to low\n70s across the lowlands, with mid 70s expected Tuesday/Wednesday\nin advance of the next system, which should provide a better \nchance of rain towards Thursday.",
